# Recorded sensor data — keep raw CSVs out of git unless you deliberately commit one
# data/* rather than data/ so specific subpaths (data/real/, data/sim/) can be
# re-included below -- a bare directory exclusion cannot be overridden by a file
# negation.
data/*
*.csv

# ...except cal_data/: the calibration dataset is hours of bench captures with
# ~40-min rest intervals between trials, not practically reproducible, and it is
# the tracked input to the committed gain-match derivation. Keep it in git.
!cal_data/*.csv

# ...and except data/real/: the first measured-position gait dataset (stand /
# walk / fast / shuffle; _01 fault set + _02 good set). The data/ rule above
# excludes the whole directory, and a file cannot be re-included while its
# parent directory is excluded -- so re-include the directory first, then its
# CSVs. check_all.csv is a scratch capture and is deliberately kept ignored.
!data/real/
!data/real/*.csv
data/real/check_all.csv

# ...and data/sim/: the five unnumbered sim_*.txt from gait_gen.py are committed
# regression fixtures. tests/test_stances.py scores against them and the
# notebook's Colab bootstrap rebuilds every sim_*.csv from them after a fresh
# clone; ignoring them would leave a clone with nothing to rebuild from.
# Everything else in there is generated and rebuilds byte-identical or is
# derived: sim_*.csv, the seeded sim_<label>_<NN>.txt sessions from
# make_sessions.py, and features_sessions.csv from scripts/bakeoff.py.
!data/sim/
data/sim/*
!data/sim/sim_walk.txt
!data/sim/sim_fast.txt
!data/sim/sim_shuffle.txt
!data/sim/sim_dropout.txt
!data/sim/sim_stand.txt

# Jupyter
.ipynb_checkpoints/
*-checkpoint.ipynb
.virtual_documents/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
build/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# VS Code
.vscode/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Local tooling and notes. None of these belong in the repository.
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
.cursor*
.aider*

# The analysis notebook writes its stance animation to the cwd (repo root).
/stance.gif
